# C2-S04 / S06 / S07 and the Ironhold ambient + camp conversations.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 2206–2306, 2719–2848.
# Scene: scenes/regions/ironhold_region.tscn. One node per NPC; the
# dispatcher nodes pick a line by story state, so each visit says something new.
# Source fix: the old "Engineer Mira" is gone (Mira Chen is Kaelen's Earth
# contact), and Seraphina no longer lectures about Root Access before meeting him.
# rhythm: clipped convoy
# (Seraphina counting heads under pressure. The short lines are the point.)

# ── Rook (market) — C2-S07 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

~ rook
[if not ch2_rook_met] => rook_first
[if not ch2_market_visited] => rook_market
=> rook_repeat

~ rook_first
set ch2_rook_met
Rook: You're the one the Commander walked through the gate. Half the market's already running odds on what you cost her.
Kaelen: Cost her? I haven't even bought anything yet.
Rook: Credibility, mostly. Rook. I move things from where they're cheap to where they aren't, and right now you're very cheap. Nothing personal.
=> rook_market

~ rook_market
set ch2_market_visited
Rook: Here's the first rule, and I'm giving it away free, which I never do. Buy low.
Kaelen: Sell high. Where I'm from, they print that one on mugs.
Rook: So you've got markets where you come from. You've got the look of someone who's been robbed by one.
Kaelen: Big ones. Screens full of numbers going up and down all night, and nobody could ever tell you why.
Rook: Then you already know the real first rule. The one they don't print on the mugs.
Kaelen: There's always a fee. Somebody's always standing in the middle, taking a cut.
# He smiles like he didn't mean to.
Rook: I might like you. Don't let it go to your head.
Rook: Prices here move with the roads, the season, and who's been nice to whom. Auction board's over there, if you'd like to lose money slowly.
[if ch2_medicine_quest_active and not ch2_medicine_done] Rook: And don't buy healing resin today. If that convoy's late, whoever's sitting on resin gets rich off sick people. This city remembers who did that.

~ rook_repeat
[if not ch2_medicine_done] Rook: Resin's up again. Somebody in this market's praying that convoy's late. I'd sell you his name, but you'd only do something decent with it.
[if ch2_medicine_done] Rook: Convoy came in, resin dropped, and three men I can't stand lost a fortune. I'm buying the first round tonight, and they're not invited.

# ── The street — C2-S04 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

~ preacher
[if ch2_administrator_proxy_defeated] => preacher_after_proxy
Preacher: The tower counts our sins! Every stroke of that bell, another one written down!
Citizen: It counts minutes, preacher. I'd know. The foundry docks me for every one I'm late.
Preacher: Then the foundry's doing the tower's work, brother, and doesn't even know it!

~ preacher_after_proxy
Citizen: Say what you like about the Proxy, there wasn't a pickpocket in the market while it was running.
Citizen: There wasn't anyone in the market. Hard to lift a purse off people who've stopped coming out.
Preacher: Then what was it counting all those years?

~ garro
Garro: Root Access can't sharpen steel, whatever else it does. Mind the quench barrel.
Kaelen: I wasn't going to say it could. I was just watching you work.
Garro: Watch from over there, then. I've got apprentices enough who think they can do my job.

~ sol
Sol: Lot twelve! One compass, from before the Fracture!
Kaelen: Does it still point north?
Sol: It points somewhere, friend, and the same somewhere every time, which is more than the roads manage! Do I hear an opening bid?

~ dice
Dice Host: Dice? Three silver a throw. Honest house, mostly, and the bell's a while off yet.
Elara: No. Keep walking.
Kaelen: I didn't say anything.
Elara: You slowed down. Nobody slows down past a dice table unless they're counting their coins.

~ doss
[if ch2_medicine_done] Doss: Resin! Cheap! Cheaper than this morning, I swear! I've a cellar full of it, please!
[if not ch2_medicine_done] Doss: Healing resin, last few jars! Price goes up every hour that convoy's out, so buy now, not at the bell!

~ paladins
[if ch2_data_wraith_restored] => paladins_restored
[if ch2_data_wraith_destroyed] => paladins_destroyed
Paladin: The Commander slept. On the wall, end of the night shift, standing up. I saw it with my own eyes.
Nori: Prove it, or that's your latrine duty for the week.
Paladin: Her eyes were closed. For ages. Long enough to count to twenty.
Seraphina: I blinked.
[if ch2_underground_unlocked] Nori: Lower streets are sealed past the market stairs. If you're going down, take somebody who knows the way back up.

~ paladins_restored
Worker: Iven woke up this morning. First time in years. Asked for his breakfast like he'd only nodded off.
Nori: Which Iven? There's three of them on my roster.
Worker: That's the trouble. He answers to all three and doesn't seem sure about any of them.

~ paladins_destroyed
Rem: The tunnels are quiet now. Nothing moving down there.
Rem: I thought quiet would feel better than this.

# ── Healer Rem and the medicine convoy — C2-S06 (time-sensitive) ──────────
# Deadline: the evening bell. In this build the bell is the Clock Tower
# stopping (clock_tower.dlg "bell"), which happens when the player goes up the
# tower. Early = before the arena's bronze bracket is won; on time = before the bell;
# late = after it (the region sets ch2_medicine_early / _on_time / _late).

~ rem
[if ch2_medicine_done] => rem_after
[if ch2_medicine_quest_active] => rem_waiting
Rem: You're the Commander's outsider. Good. I need somebody who isn't on a duty roster.
Rem: There's fever in the lower city. The medicine's on a convoy out west, stuck behind a fractured road.
Kaelen: How long do they have? The ones with the fever.
Rem: Until the evening bell. After that the gates close, and the fever does what it likes.
? Kaelen (Internal): A convoy stuck behind a broken road, and fever in the lower city waiting on it.
- I'll go now. Tell them it's coming. => rem_go_now
- I'll get there. Soon, I promise. => rem_later

~ rem_go_now
set ch2_medicine_quest_active
do quest_start medicine_convoy
Rem: West road. Take the Commander if she'll come. She always comes.

~ rem_later
set ch2_medicine_quest_active
do quest_start medicine_convoy
Rem: "Soon" is a word I hear a lot in here. West road. Before the bell.

~ rem_waiting
Rem: Evening bell. West road. I'm not going to keep saying it nicely.

~ rem_after
[if ch2_medicine_early] Rem: You got it here early. If this city does something stupid tonight, I'll have beds to spare.
[if ch2_medicine_on_time] Rem: In time. That's all I ask of anyone, and hardly anyone manages it.
[if ch2_medicine_late] Rem: It came. After the bell. Tomas and the Wren girl are still burning up. Don't apologise to me. Apologise to them when they can hear you.
Kaelen: Those blue potions you hand out. What do you call them?
Rem: Breath. Because that's what they give back.
Kaelen: That's better than ours. Ours had a number and a warning on the back.

# The escort, on the west road (region story gate). Seraphina counts.
~ convoy
do fade_to_road
Seraphina: Forty-two.
Kaelen: You keep counting them. They haven't gone anywhere.
Seraphina: Forty-two people. Six wagons.
Kaelen: People before wagons. Every time.
Seraphina: Wagons don't wander off. Wagon three, sit down for me, please.
Kaelen: You said it like that on the plane. "For me, please."
Seraphina: Don't.
Kaelen: Sorry. I didn't—
# She nods. She doesn't stop counting.
do convoy_ambush
Seraphina: Forty-two. All of them.
[if ch2_seraphina_truth] => convoy_count
=> convoy_done

~ convoy_count
Seraphina: I counted then, too. Afterwards. Row by row, the way they train you.
Seraphina: I stopped at one hundred and eighty-six.
# Kaelen says nothing. It's the right thing to say.
Seraphina: There were more.
set ch2_seraphina_186_told
=> convoy_done

~ convoy_done
set ch2_medicine_done
do trust seraphina 10

# ── Seraphina off duty (city NPC) and the camp conversations ──────────────

~ seraphina
[if not ch2_ks_01_done] => ks_01
[if not ch2_es_01_done] => es_01
[if ch2_medicine_done and not ch2_ks_02_done] => ks_02
[if ch2_arena_bronze_complete and not ch2_es_02_done] => es_02
[if ch2_clock_tower_complete and not ch2_ks_03_done] => ks_03
[if ch2_clock_tower_complete and not ch2_es_03_done] => es_03
=> seraphina_idle

~ ks_01
set ch2_ks_01_done
Kaelen: Do you remember the impact? The actual moment?
Seraphina: Yes. Every part of it. I could draw you the cabin.
Kaelen: I don't. There's a gap, and then I'm lying in a crater.
Seraphina: Don't be jealous.

~ ks_02
set ch2_ks_02_done
Seraphina: You had coffee.
Kaelen: On the plane?
Seraphina: Before boarding. You spilled it down your sleeve.
Kaelen: That's a weirdly specific thing to remember.
Seraphina: I spent the first hour of the flight trying not to look at the stain.

~ ks_03
set ch2_ks_03_done
Kaelen: Why a paladin? Of everything you could've been here.
Seraphina: The armour was available.
Kaelen: That's the whole reason? It was in stock?
Seraphina: At first. Then people started listening to me.
Kaelen: Why did they listen to you?
Seraphina: Because frightened people want someone to tell them where to stand, and I'd been doing that for years before any of this.

~ es_01
set ch2_es_01_done
Seraphina: Your arm's getting worse.
Elara: Everyone's an expert on my arm lately.
Seraphina: I was trained. Long before the armour.
Elara: To watch arms? What kind of trade trains you for that?
Seraphina: To watch people pretending they're fine.
# Elara looks away.
Elara: Then watch the road instead. It's the thing getting worse.

~ es_02
set ch2_es_02_done
Elara: Flight attendant. That's what he called you.
Seraphina: Yes.
Elara: You served food. In the sky.
Seraphina: Among other things. Mostly I asked people to sit down. Nicely, the first time.
Elara: And then you became Knight-Commander.
Seraphina: Career change.
Elara: That isn't a career change. I don't think there's a word for what that is.

~ es_03
set ch2_es_03_done
Seraphina: Is he always like this?
Elara: Kaelen? Like what, exactly?
Seraphina: Who else?
Elara: Worse when he's scared. Then he explains everything, in order, whether you asked or not.
Kaelen: I'm standing right here. I can hear every word.
Elara: Hear that? He's gone polite. That's the scared voice.

~ seraphina_idle
[if ch2_administrator_proxy_defeated] Seraphina: Brask wants a report on the Proxy. I've written "it was running the city" three times. He keeps sending it back.
[if not ch2_administrator_proxy_defeated] Seraphina: I've been up since the second bell, and I'm here until the next one. If I fall asleep standing, salute me.

~ ina
Ina: Knight-Commander!
Seraphina: Off duty, Ina. And walk, please. Nobody runs past the forges.
Ina: But if you're off duty, are you still a knight? Or are you just Seraphina?
Seraphina: Both. The knight part doesn't come off with the armour. I've tried.

~ vex
Vex: Arena's open! Bring your teeth, take home fewer!

# Before the Clock Tower: the convoy's deadline is the bell (fair warning).
~ tower_warning
Seraphina: The convoy's still out on the west road. When that tower rings again, the gates close behind it.
? Kaelen (Internal): The convoy's still out there, and the bell won't wait for it. Go up anyway?
- Not yet. Convoy first, then the tower. => END
- Up now. The convoy will have to wait. => tower_go

~ tower_go
set ch2_tower_go_now
